1
00:00:00,070 --> 00:00:01,036
You scratch your cat

2
00:00:01,036 --> 00:00:02,400
and she purrs.

3
00:00:02,400 --> 00:00:03,062
Happy cat,

4
00:00:03,062 --> 00:00:03,710
RIGHT?

5
00:00:03,710 --> 00:00:04,313
Maybe,

6
00:00:04,313 --> 00:00:05,331
but scientists think

7
00:00:05,331 --> 00:00:07,050
a purr really means...

8
00:00:07,050 --> 00:00:08,033
look after me.

9
00:00:08,320 --> 00:00:09,153
Her voice box

10
00:00:09,153 --> 00:00:09,730
flutters

11
00:00:09,730 --> 00:00:11,450
twenty-five times a second,

12
00:00:11,450 --> 00:00:12,450
breathing in

13
00:00:12,450 --> 00:00:13,533
AND out.

14
00:00:13,560 --> 00:00:14,490
Kittens start

15
00:00:14,490 --> 00:00:15,954
days after birth,

16
00:00:15,954 --> 00:00:17,700
eyes still shut.

17
00:00:17,750 --> 00:00:18,904
Grown cats purr

18
00:00:18,904 --> 00:00:20,210
when they're happy...

19
00:00:20,210 --> 00:00:21,333
or HURT.

20
00:00:21,460 --> 00:00:22,320
And hungry?

21
00:00:22,320 --> 00:00:23,332
She hides a cry

22
00:00:23,332 --> 00:00:24,240
inside it,

23
00:00:24,240 --> 00:00:25,028
pitched like

24
00:00:25,028 --> 00:00:27,150
a human baby's.

25
00:00:27,380 --> 00:00:29,260
You don't own a cat.

26
00:00:29,260 --> 00:00:30,550
You're staff.

